  "id": "blank-screen",
  "term": "blank screen",
  "definition": "In this cognition research context, a blank screen is a neutral visual display that participants look at during memory recall instead of closing their eyes or viewing distracting sights or sounds. It serves as a low-distraction comparison condition when studying how visual input affects remembering.",
